WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.000
Speaker 1: Criminal defense lawyer wrote to
me over the weekend, tears in his eyes, I

00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:07.319
could tell, even though it was an email that
the guy was crying as he wrote to me and he

00:00:07.319 --> 00:00:10.120
said, David, listen, I'm a criminal defense
attorney.

00:00:10.120 --> 00:00:18.430
Where Trump can get himself into real trouble
here is if he has a gag order placed on him

00:00:18.430 --> 00:00:23.880
at tomorrow's arraignment, he may not be able
to resist talking about the case, and that

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:29.080
would be considered a bond violation and it
could get Trump rearrested.

00:00:29.080 --> 00:00:35.700
The latest news is that a gag order is, quote,
extremely likely at tomorrow's arraignment.

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.660
And Donald Trump has scheduled a press conference
for tomorrow evening.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:39.660
Okay.

00:00:39.660 --> 00:00:46.370
So this has this is a secondary story which
has the potential to completely explode into

00:00:46.370 --> 00:00:52.649
a very different sort of situation than this
coordinated, very dignified arrest that is

00:00:52.649 --> 00:00:54.879
taking place tomorrow in New York City.

00:00:54.879 --> 00:00:56.140
Business Insider Report.

00:00:56.140 --> 00:00:57.140
Quartz.

00:00:57.140 --> 00:00:58.309
Let's go through it piece by piece.

00:00:58.309 --> 00:01:02.470
A gag order for Donald Trump is extremely
likely once he's before a judge.

00:01:02.470 --> 00:01:07.720
Legal expert says Donald Trump can't seem
to stop talking about his indictment, but

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.030
he may have to soon.

00:01:10.030 --> 00:01:14.070
It's extremely likely he'll be put under gag
order, one expert said.

00:01:14.070 --> 00:01:21.210
Punishment in New York for criminal contempt
could be a $1,000 fine or 30 days in jail.

00:01:21.210 --> 00:01:25.700
Such a gag order would say to Trump and others
involved in the case do not speak publicly

00:01:25.700 --> 00:01:27.409
about the case.

00:01:27.409 --> 00:01:32.530
And yet an announcement from yesterday that
Donald Trump tomorrow will be holding a press

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:35.970
conference about the arraignment in Mar a
Lago.

00:01:35.970 --> 00:01:41.579
The announcement coming on Trump Make America
Great Again 2024 letterhead, naturally.

00:01:41.579 --> 00:01:44.399
And it says Tuesday, April four, 815 Eastern.

00:01:44.399 --> 00:01:46.229
That's tomorrow evening.

00:01:46.229 --> 00:01:50.790
President Donald J. Trump, 45th president
of the United States, will deliver remarks

00:01:50.790 --> 00:01:55.619
at Mar a Lago in Palm Beach, Florida, at 815.

00:01:55.619 --> 00:01:59.479
This is expected to be not only remarks, but
a press conference.

00:01:59.479 --> 00:02:05.720
If there is a gag order and Donald Trump doesn't
cancel that event and he speaks about the

00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:07.689
case against him.

00:02:07.689 --> 00:02:09.599
He would be subject to re-arrest.

00:02:09.599 --> 00:02:13.890
Now, I know people are saying 30 days in jail
with Trump.

00:02:13.890 --> 00:02:16.019
It would probably be the thousand dollar fine.

00:02:16.019 --> 00:02:17.150
Let's be completely honest.

00:02:17.150 --> 00:02:19.819
But it would make him subject to re-arrest.

00:02:19.819 --> 00:02:23.460
And in all seriousness, none of them were
crying when they emailed me that I know of.

00:02:23.460 --> 00:02:28.670
But numerous lawyers wrote to me and said,
This is really where Trump has to be careful.

00:02:28.670 --> 00:03:15.390
The next question mark, which I believe is
of utter importance, is whether this arraignment

00:03:15.390 --> 00:03:41.870
will 

00:03:41.870 --> 00:03:51.170
be televised.

